# ---- build trees -----------------------------------------------------------
build/
build-*/
*.o
*.a
*.so
*.so.*
CMakeCache.txt
CMakeFiles/

# ---- models ----------------------------------------------------------------
# Shipped solver models under models/milp/ are tracked.
models/**/*.bak

# ---- Python ----------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
web/.venv/

# External-solver baselines (HiGHS / SciPy / PuLP). NEVER commit: the venv
# contains libhighs.so, and shipping a competitor solver's binary would
# contradict the clean-room boundary in docs/architecture.md §8. Recreate with:
#   python3 -m venv benchmarks/.venv-baseline
#   benchmarks/.venv-baseline/bin/pip install -r benchmarks/requirements-baseline.txt
benchmarks/.venv-baseline/

# ---- competitor log files written into the working tree --------------------
# highspy drops this in the CWD on every run.
Highs.log

# ---- generated run outputs -------------------------------------------------
demo_out/
nohup.out
*.out
*.log

# ---- downloaded benchmark instances ---------------------------------------
# Public benchmark models are fetched selectively rather than committed:
#   python3 scripts/fetch_benchmarks.py --list
#   python3 scripts/fetch_benchmarks.py --suite netlib --instance afiro
#   python3 scripts/fetch_benchmarks.py --suite miplib-easy
benchmarks/netlib/
benchmarks/miplib-easy/mps/
benchmarks/miplib2017/mps/
benchmarks/miplib2017/*.zip

# Synthetic scaling-study LPs (generated, up to ~150 MB each). Regenerate:
#   python3 scripts/gen_lp_ladder.py
benchmarks/synthetic/mps/

# ---- benchmark RESULTS (ignore all; force-add the citable runs) ------------
# Promote a run with:  git add -f benchmarks/results/<stamp>.md <stamp>.jsonl
benchmarks/results/*
!benchmarks/results/compare-netlib-20260905-140353.md
!benchmarks/results/compare-netlib-20260905-140353.jsonl
!benchmarks/results/miplib-easy-20260905-141554.md
!benchmarks/results/miplib-easy-20260905-141554.jsonl

# Third-party papers read for the clean-room work (docs/paper_bibliography.md
# cites them by DOI/arXiv). 38 MB of published PDFs, so they are kept locally
# rather than redistributed through this repository's history.
docs/papers/

# Local Netlib emps binary (source: benchmarks/netlib/raw/emps.c)
benchmarks/tools/

# ---- QP work: kept locally, not shipped -------------------------------------
# Working notes, superseded status documents, generated pooling instances and
# sweep output. QP.md at the repository root carries what a reader needs; the
# generators under scripts/ are seeded, so every generated instance is
# reproducible from the command recorded there.
docs/agent-notes/
docs/ENGINE_PARITY.md
docs/QP_STATUS.md
docs/REFINERY.md
docs/THIRD_PARTY.md
docs/WORK_PLAN.md
benchmarks/refinery/
benchmarks/reference/
benchmarks/qplib/
# QP generators, sweep drivers and fetchers. scripts/qplib_eval.py stays: the
# registered test_qplib_eval loads it at runtime, so it is a build dependency.
scripts/compare_reference.py
scripts/fetch_qplib.py
scripts/fetch_qplib_all.py
scripts/fetch_qplib_varnames.py
scripts/gen_qp_ladder.py
scripts/pooling_gen.py
scripts/qp_crossover.py
scripts/qplib_all_sweep.py
scripts/qplib_global_sweep.py
scripts/qplib_miqp_sweep.py
scripts/qplib_parse_all.py
scripts/qplib_sweep.py
scripts/refinery_bench.py

# superseded by QP_PERFS.md
QPLIB_TIMING.md
